## Problem

The app crashes at runtime with:
```
java.lang.ClassCastException: java.lang.Class cannot be cast to java.lang.reflect.ParameterizedType
```

This happens when Retrofit tries to resolve the return type of suspend functions like:
```kotlin
suspend fun login(@Body request: LoginRequest): Response<ApiResponse<AuthResponse>>
```

The crash occurs because R8 (minification enabled in release builds with `isMinifyEnabled = true` in `android/app/build.gradle.kts` line 38) strips the generic type signature metadata that Retrofit needs to resolve `Response<ApiResponse<AuthResponse>>` at runtime via reflection.

## Root Cause

R8 in "full mode" (the default when using `proguard-android-optimize.txt`) strips generic signatures from classes/interfaces not explicitly kept by a `-keep` rule — even when `-keepattributes Signature` is present. Retrofit 2.9.0's suspend function support works by inspecting `Continuation<Response<ApiResponse<T>>>` parameter types via reflection. When R8 strips the `Signature` attribute from `kotlin.coroutines.Continuation`, `retrofit2.Response`, and `retrofit2.Call`, Retrofit sees a raw `Class` instead of a `ParameterizedType` and throws this `ClassCastException`.

## Fix Required

Update `android/app/proguard-rules.pro` (currently at commit `a602b2ac751c1f9f00e32391e6b0c46547375fdb`, BlobSha `fb90a77c0c71afc167ffedd0b5697d630f9aefa6`) to add the official Retrofit R8 full-mode keep rules.

The current file content is:
```proguard
